---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../../../components/Section.astro';
import { ROUTES, SITE } from '../../../consts';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const updated = '2026-09-30';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — MILLIMETER by Casanova"
  description="What data we collect, why, who we share it with, and how to exercise your rights."
  lang={lang}
  noindex
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title={['Privacy', 'policy.']} measure={`Updated ${updated}`} />

  <Section measure="§" label="Privacy">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This document describes <strong>exactly</strong> what this site does with your data.
        It is written against the site's actual code, not a template: if a processing
        activity is not listed here, it does not happen.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>{SITE.controller.name}</strong>, a company incorporated in
        {' '}{SITE.controller.state}, {SITE.controller.countryEn}, based in
        {' '}{SITE.controller.city}.
      </p>
      <p>
        The South America representation acts on behalf of this company and is not a
        separate legal entity. Enquiries sent from this site go directly to the company's
        corporate mailbox.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Contact channel for anything concerning your data</strong>, including
        exercising your rights:
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>When</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Name</td><td>Contact form</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email</td><td>Contact form</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Studio or company</td><td>Contact form</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Country</td><td>Contact form</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Professional role</td><td>Contact form</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Message content</td><td>Contact form</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Name and email</td><td>Careers form</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Country of residence, area of interest and introduction</td><td>Careers form</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Résumé (PDF file, with everything it contains)</td><td>Careers form</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>IP address</td><td>Every visit, in server logs</td><td>Automatic</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        <strong>We use no third-party analytics</strong>, no advertising pixels, no
        profiling, no automated decision-making. There is no Google Analytics, no Meta Pixel,
        no heatmaps. We do not sell or share data with third parties for commercial purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To answer your enquiry</strong> and continue the commercial conversation you started.</li>
        <li><strong>To assess your application</strong>, if you send one through the careers form, and to contact you about the selection process.</li>
        <li><strong>Site security</strong>: the IP address is used to rate-limit form submissions and stop automated abuse.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The legal basis is your <strong>explicit consent</strong> when submitting the form
        (an unticked checkbox you tick yourself) and our <strong>legitimate interest</strong>
        in keeping the site running and free of abuse. For the careers form, consent expressly
        covers processing your résumé for the selection process.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Résumé</strong>: we only accept PDF files. Please do not include data that is not
        needed to assess your profile (ID numbers, photographs of third parties, health data).
        We will process whatever the file contains exactly as you send it.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>Only the providers strictly required for the site to work:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Function</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Railway</td><td>Site hosting and server logs</td><td>United States</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Email delivery of the contact and careers forms, including the attached résumé</td><td>United States</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GoDaddy</td><td>Domain registration and DNS</td><td>United States</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WhatsApp (Meta)</td><td>Only if you press the WhatsApp button: the chat opens in their app</td><td>United States and others</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        <strong>The WhatsApp button is a plain link</strong>: this site loads nothing from WhatsApp or
        Meta while you browse. WhatsApp only opens if you press it, and from then on your number and your
        message are handled by WhatsApp under its own policy, not by this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        This involves an <strong>international transfer</strong> of data to the United States.
        If you live somewhere whose law requires specific safeguards for such transfers,
        write to us and we will detail the ones that apply.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Form enquiries</strong>: for the duration of the commercial conversation and up to 24 months after the last contact.</li>
        <li><strong>Applications and résumés</strong>: for the duration of the selection process and <strong>12 months</strong> at most from receipt, unless you ask us to delete them sooner.</li>
        <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: retained by Railway under its own retention policy.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookie-notice preference</strong>: in your browser until you clear site data. It never leaves your device.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask us at any time for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong>: what data of yours we hold.</li>
        <li><strong>Rectification</strong>: correct anything wrong.</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure</strong>: delete everything we have on you.</li>
        <li><strong>Objection and restriction</strong> of processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Portability</strong>: receive your data in a readable format.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong>, without affecting prior processing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> from the address you
        contacted us with. We reply within 30 calendar days. There is no charge and we will
        not ask you to justify the request.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe we have not handled your request properly, you can complain to the
        data protection authority in your country.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Security</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>All site traffic is encrypted over HTTPS.</li>
        <li>The form validates and length-limits every field on the server, not just in the browser.</li>
        <li>Per-IP rate limiting stops automated submissions.</li>
        <li>The site sends security headers, including a restrictive Content Security Policy.</li>
        <li>We store nothing in a database of our own: the enquiry or application travels by email and lives in the destination inbox.</li>
        <li><strong>The résumé is not stored on the website</strong>: it is processed in memory, checked and sent by email. Only PDF is accepted, up to 5 MB; the file's content is verified (not just its extension), PDFs with active content (scripts, embedded attachments) are rejected, and the file is renamed before it is sent.</li>
        <li>The careers form has a stricter per-IP submission limit than the contact form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Minors</h2>
      <p>
        This site is aimed at architecture, design and construction professionals. It is not
        intended for minors and we do not knowingly collect their data.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If anything material changes — for example if analytics are ever added — this page and
        its date are updated. The version in force is always the one published here.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      <p><a href={ROUTES.cookies.en}>See also: cookie policy</a></p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
